<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25737" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lămus</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάμος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mythic king of the Læstrygonians, a son
				of Neptune, and the founder of Formiæ</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				17, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8, 530</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence, urbs Lami,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Formiæ</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 233</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A son of Hercules and Omphale</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 9,
			54</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The name of a horse</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 16,
				474</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
